  "scope": "Constructed volume-preserving Euclidean coordinates and an actual unitary six-dimensional Fourier map for the coupled configuration Hilbert space. The full longitudinal group becomes multiplication by exp(2*pi*i*t*k0). The actual self-adjoint momentum graph is exactly multiplication by 2*pi*hbar*k0 in these coordinates, and its maximal domain is exactly the states with that weighted Fourier transform in L2. A proved strong/pointwise derivative comparison and self-adjointness supply the two graph inclusions; no multiplier-domain assumption is used. The exponential operator and its full form domain, a spatial smooth core, full Hamiltonian terms, charge averaging, finite-to-infinite identification, controlled limits, physical identification and the TOE remain open."
}
